Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Permission Denied Errors
If you encounter permission denied errors:

# Check if the role exists
kubectl get role <role-name> -n <namespace>

# Check if the rolebinding exists
kubectl get rolebinding <rolebinding-name> -n <namespace>

# Verify the user has the correct permissions
kubectl auth can-i <verb> <resource> --as=<user> -n <namespace>
Issue 2: Service Account Token Issues
If service account tokens are not working:

# Check if the service account exists
kubectl get serviceaccount <sa-name> -n <namespace>

# Check if the service account has secrets
kubectl describe serviceaccount <sa-name> -n <namespace>

# Manually create a token if needed (Kubernetes 1.24+)
kubectl create token <sa-name> -n <namespace>
Issue 3: Role Not Taking Effect
If roles are not taking effect:

# Check the role definition
kubectl describe role <role-name> -n <namespace>

# Check the rolebinding
kubectl describe rolebinding <rolebinding-name> -n <namespace>

# Verify API groups and resources
kubectl api-resources | grep kubevirt
